= Open access — Technical =

Open access has separable dimensions: reader cost, immediacy, repository availability, machine accessibility, and legal reuse permissions. A work can be free to read while carrying restrictive reuse terms, so access status and license status should not be collapsed.

== Modeling / implementation cautions ==
* open access ≠ open science
* free-to-read ≠ unrestricted reuse necessarily
* open access ≠ absence of copyright

== References ==
* Budapest Open Access Initiative (2002), foundational open-access statement.
* Berlin Declaration on Open Access to Knowledge in the Sciences and Humanities (2003).
* UNESCO, “What is Open Access?”, current resource.
